###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Force, energy and dipole RMSEs for all models (Figs. 7-13, S1-S5) are figure-only; the text states no numeric errors. Training-dynamics comparisons, slab polarization and defect relaxations (Tables V-VI) are properties.
# - All variants are encoded as MACE runs: the paper builds every model on the MACE framework and does not name the energy-functional or fixed-point architectures as new methods. MACE-LocalCharges is described as almost identical to MACE-LES (except higher-order multipoles and linear charges) but is not mapped to it. Whether the self-consistent architectures deserve their own registry methods is left for review.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/baldwin2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
